  "text": "Mobile Vet Oncologist In South FL | Pompano Vet Oncology\nHablamos Español\n…\n\n754-281-8893\n…\n…\n\n…\n\nHome\nAbout\nOur Story\nOur Team\nReviews\nPhoto Gallery\nServices\nMobile Service\nCancer Consultation\nDiagnosis & Staging\nCancer Treatment\nHome Euthanasia\nResources\nWhy Animals Get Cancer\nPayment Options\nContact\nAppointment\nCLINICAL TRIALS: **TEMPORARILY PAUSED**\nNow offering\nAT HOME\nRadiation Therapy.\n1. IMMUNOTHERAPY FOR DOGS WITH SOLID TUMORS: SARCOMAS AND CARCINOMAS\n2.\nINTRATUMORAL IMMUNOTHERAPY AND ELECTROPORATION FOR SOFT TISSUE SARCOMAS\nNOTE: Partially and fully funded clinical studies available\nBroward County & Palm Beach, FL\nWelcome To Pompano Veterinary Oncology\nAt\nPompano Veterinary Oncology\n, we have a big heart for our patients. We are committed to creating a liaison between primary care veterinarians, pet owners, and\nour veterinary team\nwith the ultimate goal of advancing the fight against\nfeline and canine cancer.\nAppointment\nFull Cancer Treatment – at Home\nWe understand that cancer can be a challenging time for you and your pet. With this in mind, we offer at-home services/house calls for\nfeline and canine cancer\n. We are fully equipped for diagnostics and offer the same treatment and quality as “in-clinic”. Additionally, with our mobile oncology, we minimize patient stress in a convenient, efficient service.\nRadiation Therapy\nWe now offer the world’s first mobile, accurate, and customized radiation therapy. Radiation therapy’s function in treating veterinary cancer is changing. New levels of cancer patient care for ailing pets are being made possible by the growing use of more sophisticated technology and cancer treatments.\nAbout Pompano Veterinary Oncology\nAt\nPompano Veterinary Oncology\n, quality\nveterinary care\nis our top priority. We are committed to:\nProviding high-quality\ncancer treatment for companion animals\n.\nPromoting the health and safety of our patients.\nProviding our clients with expert advice, information about their pet’s health, and available treatment options.\nProviding appropriate, innovative, and logical treatment to exceed expectations.\nCreating a community where our clients can connect with others in similar situations is vital. We strive to foster an environment of support and camaraderie.\nMore about us\nComplete Veterinary Oncology Care\nWith recent advances in\ncanine and feline cancer treatment\n, clients and their companion animals have more options and hope than ever when fighting cancer. At\nPompano Veterinary Oncology\n, our clients receive high-quality treatment options with the compassion that they would expect for their pet family. Learn more about our medical oncology services below.\nMobile Service\nDetails →\nConsultation for Cancer\nDetails →\nDiagnosis and staging\nDetails →\nFeline and Canine Cancer\nDetails →\nView All services\nMeet Our Veterinary Team at Pompano Veterinary Oncology\nAt\nPompano Veterinary Oncology\n, we are committed to advancing the fight against cancer in companion animals. Our\nveterinary team\nbelieves that treating\ncanine and feline cancer\nis not just a matter of addressing their medical needs – we believe it is important to create a community where our clients can connect with others in similar situations, which fosters an environment of support and camaraderie. Pets with cancer need more than direct cancer treatment, and our experienced vet team is here to help.\nMeet the team\nWe love our clients and patients!\nThank you for making us a top-rated veterinarian in\nPalm Beach\n, FL. Your kind words mean the world to us, and we appreciate you taking the time to leave us a review.\nRead Reviews\nSchedule An Appointment Today!\nWe proudly serve companion animals in\nBroward County and Palm Beach County.\nBook Appointment\n\nLocation\n353 SW 13th Ave\nPompano Beach, Fl 33069\n\nContact Information\nPhone:\n754-281-8893\n\nHours\nMonday-Wednesday:\n8 AM – 4 PM\nThursday & Friday:\n8 AM – 12 PM\nSaturday:\nClosed\nSunday:\nClosed\n© 2026 Pompano Veterinary Oncology |\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nPowered by PetDesk\nFollow\nFollow",
